⑩00000052⑿
易考范文二十三
⑩00000468⑿
As is depicted in the above drawing, a waiter,
⑩00000971⑿
using “payment in advance” as a preferential measure,
⑩00001354⑿
sets a trap for the customer in reality.
⑩00001671⑿
What is revealed in the drawing is a social phenomenon that
⑩00002054⑿
has aroused nationwide concerns.
⑩00002339⑿
Nowadays, in order to attract more customers,
⑩00002677⑿
a great number of businessmen adopt the favorable strategy of advance payment,
⑩00003257⑿
promising that consumers are entitled to discounts
⑩00003629⑿
as long as they pay for the service beforehand.
⑩00003925⑿
As can be expected, many a consumer can hardly resist those tempting discounts
⑩00004548⑿
and pays a large sum of money in advance.
⑩00004854⑿
However, instead of keeping their word to offer service,
⑩00005259⑿
some businessmen flee with the money they swindle out of the customers,
⑩00005718⑿
while the latter have to accept bad luck.
⑩00010025⑿
I assume this hard nut can be cracked in light of the following aspects.
⑩00010527⑿
First of all, consumers should be more cautious
⑩00010899⑿
and pay more attention to the credit of the shop.
⑩00011184⑿
Secondly, the Consumer's Association is supposed to take effective measures
⑩00011709⑿
to protect the consumers' rights.
⑩00011939⑿
What's more, it is vital for the businessmen to realize that
⑩00012354⑿
conning consumers can do most harm to nobody but themselves in the end
⑩00012857⑿
and that they'd better win a good credit for the sake of long-run profit.
